SEL: ``peat push -d selrelay`` can push a QuickSet database (``*.rdb``), a ``SET_ALL.TXT``, a single settings file, or a directory of settings files (filenames are case-insensitive). They're converted into the per-class settings files (``SET_1.TXT``, ``SET_P1.TXT``, ...), which are saved and hashed in the device results (``push_SET_ALL.txt`` and ``push_files/``) before connecting, so they're kept even if the push fails or is refused. The relay in a RDB file is chosen with the new ``sel.push_rdb_relay`` option, or by matching the device.
